name w2-03-radius
timeout 6700
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 3 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE RANGE RIDE, CLEAN. THE NUMBER EVERYTHING ELSE IN THIS CAMPAIGN IS MEASURED AGAINST.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control of w2-04-loaded.fbm (ONE fact: two Mk-84 on stations 3 and 7).
# Callsigns are disjoint between the two, per O4's rule: the store carry is keyed by callsign.
#
# THE ANCHOR: the package flew "over 1,600 km" for the round trip and was "near the limit of its
# range"; the external tanks were exhausted en route and jettisoned over the Saudi desert [T4]. The
# same source's own straight-line figure is ~1,090 km each way, which does not agree with its own
# round-trip number; MEASURED between the two coordinates the source itself gives (Etzion 29.94/34.87,
# Al-Tuwaitha 33.20/44.52) the great circle is 982.9 km each way, 1,965.9 km out and back [DERIVED].
# ALL THREE FIGURES ARE CARRIED. The campaign compares its measured radius against all of them and
# averages none.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: HOW FAR CAN THIS JET GO AND COME HOME, CLEAN, AT THE ANCHOR'S OWN
# INGRESS ALTITUDE? The spec's §Knowledge 2 prescribes the method and it is followed literally: "fly
# increasing legs until the jet cannot return, and declare the campaign's leg at 90 % of that". THE
# LADDER WAS FLOWN FIRST, as an attribution run outside the ten (campaign file §State):
#   240 m, 400 kt, `fuel_int_pct 100`, one straight leg to fuel exhaustion
#     clean                       FLAMEOUT AT 1,492.6 km, 4.6708 lb/km, t = 7,265.6 s
#   the same leg at 8,000 m, already committed in doc/modules/stores.md
#     clean                       FLAMEOUT AT 2,627.4 km, 2.6535 lb/km
#   -> THE ANCHOR'S OWN INGRESS ALTITUDE COSTS 43.2 % OF THE RANGE [DERIVED, 1 - 1492.6/2627.4]
# One-way flameout distance is not a radius: with no reserve and no allowance the radius is half of it,
# 746.3 km. THIS FILE FLIES 90 % OF THAT OUT AND BACK: 671.7 km each way, 1,343.4 km total [DERIVED].
#
# WHAT THE NUMBER IS NOT, STATED BEFORE IT IS READ. This jet spawns IN THE AIR at cruise altitude and
# cruise speed. The anchor's aircraft started their engines, taxied, took off and climbed on the same
# fuel, and FlightBox models none of that: EVERY W2 RANGE NUMBER IS AN UPPER BOUND on the flyable
# radius, and the direction of the error is known and one-sided.
#
# THE ARENA: the raid's own outbound track from Etzion AB 29.94000 34.87000 [T4, approximate] on
# bearing 068.37 deg, out to the 671.7 km turn point and back to Etzion. Scale: 1 deg lat = 111,320 m,
# 1 deg lon at 31.570 N = 94,845 m [DERIVED].
#   `w2pit`  target_soft  32.16405 41.41736 - a desert installation at the turn point (campaign rule 3)
#
# WHY THIS FILE DECLARES NO `kill` OBJECTIVE, AND WHY THAT IS THE DISCIPLINED CHOICE. It is the CLEAN
# control: it carries nothing to attack with. Its sibling w2-04 carries two Mk-84 and is otherwise
# identical line for line, INCLUDING ITS OBJECTIVES - so the ONE difference between the two runs is
# the two `set store` lines, and the kill is read out of `UNIT_RESULT` beside the fuel rather than out
# of an exit code that would then differ for two reasons at once.
#
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm):
#   1. `C5` half closed - the tank exists and is NOT on this jet; AERIAL REFUELLING IS NOT BUILT, so
#      nothing in this campaign says what a tanker would have been worth.
#   2. `C20` open, `--elev const`, 0 m plane; the real ground under this route is 42.83-1,599.22 m
#      (MEASURED, listed in w2-02-ingress.fbm). Etzion itself is at 523.59 m, so this jet flies its
#      whole ride 283.59 m BELOW its own airfield.
#   3. `C10` - level laydown; irrelevant here, nothing is dropped.
#   4/5/6 - no F-15, `FirstFlightKo`, W1's fixed point: all irrelevant, this is a single jet alone.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is NOT the measurement. Read, in this order: (1) `fuelLbs` in
# the LAST telemetry row - the campaign contract §2 requires every mission to report it and this is the
# file it was written for, (2) whether both `nav WP_REACHED` lines appear, (3) the ground distance
# flown. A run that lands with reserve to spare has not tested the thing this raid was about; a run
# that does not get home has answered the campaign's central question in the negative.

# MEASURED (fingerprint a97fba1ebbc02613, exit 0): THE CLEAN JET GETS HOME WITH 516.4 lb.
#   the leg       `nav WP_REACHED idx=0` at t=3,261.1 s (the 671.7 km turn point), `idx=1` at
#                 t=6,576.9 s (Etzion). 1,343.4 km flown, 204.3 m/s average ground speed
#   fuel          6,971.8 lb at t=0 -> 516.4 lb in the last row: 7.4 % of what it launched with
#   the margin    the identical file run to exhaustion instead of stopped at 6,700 s crashes at
#                 t=7,368.5 s at 29.4419/33.4037 - 152.3 km PAST its own airfield. That is the whole
#                 reserve, and it is what "near the limit of its range" is as a number here
#   Read beside w2-04-loaded.fbm, which is this file plus two `set store` lines and does NOT get home.

unit w2rad3
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 29.94000 34.87000 240 68.4 400        # Etzion AB, on the raid's own outbound bearing
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                        # 6,972 lb internal, CLEAN - no store, no tank
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 32.16405 41.41736 240 400                # THE TURN POINT: 671.7 km out = 90 % of the measured radius
  wp 29.94000 34.87000 240 400                # home, the same 671.7 km back
  objective waypoints
  objective survive

unit w2pit
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 32.16405 41.41736 ground 68.4 0
